                                                                                                                      "value":  "Earlier gaps come from when each series began, not from lost records. Starting in January 2008 leaves 1 of 1,561 monthly cells empty (0.06%), the first COLCAP return, which cannot exist without a prior month. Nothing was imputed, because filling it would invent data. The impact is one fewer observation for returns and the loss of pre-2008 history. Inflation and the policy rate have means above their medians (4.93% vs 3.97% and 6.11% vs 4.50%), pulled up by the 2022-23 cycle.",
